==English==

===Etymology===
From [[Greek]] [[μεσολιθικός]] (''mesolithikos''), from [[Ancient Greek]] prefix [[μεσο-]]
"[[meso-]]", from [[μέσος]] (''mesos'') "middle" + [[λίθος]] (''lithos'') "stone".

===Pronunciation===
mes·o·lith·ic
* SAMPA: /mĕsōlĭthīk/
MEHS-o-LITH-ik<!--
{{audio|en-int}}
{{audio|en-au}}
{{audio|en-be}}-->

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A period that lasted between 10,000 and 3,000 BC, of or relating to the [[Middle Stone Age]].

